  "intro": [
    "Every IoT Core operation the emulator advertises, and what Emuplane does with",
    "it. The control plane is REST-style \u2014 the verb and path select the action \u2014",
    "signed with the `iot` scope; `Publish` and the retained-message reads are the",
    "`iot-data` plane. The README row's own \"76 operations\" counts",
    "`MQTT-over-WebSocket pub/sub`, which is a transport rather than a callable",
    "operation, so the ledger excludes it and names the row's `Publish (HTTP)` as",
    "`Publish`: 75 callable operations.",
    "Certificates are real X.509. The suite builds its own CA and a verification",
    "certificate whose CN is the account's registration code, registers the CA, and",
    "issues leaves with it for `RegisterCertificate` and",
    "`RegisterCertificateWithoutCA`; `CreateCertificateFromCsr` signs a locally",
    "generated CSR with the emulator's local CA. Policy attachment needs a",
    "certificate target, and a custom domain configuration needs an ACM",
    "certificate, which the delete test requests. Rule actions carry a role ARN",
    "that the live `AUTH=true` evaluator resolves, so the suite creates that IAM",
    "role; the in-process stand-in does not check it. Delete tests create their own",
    "resource and update tests restore the stable record."
  ],
